TripVerse How it worksDestinationsExploreQuestionsSign in Start planning Agentic travel planningTripVerse works it out with you. Tell a guide where you are going and it drafts the days, keeps an eye on the budget, and opens the trip as a studio you can explore: a plan, a sketchbook, a map and a 3D route. Start planning Explore destinations Six guides. Pick who plans your trip with you. Seoul · 5 nightsPlanning now Read your brief Researched possible stops Checked your dates Writing your day-by-day draft Kyoto · 3 days · budget Flights, Delhi and back~₹60,000 Stay, 2 nights~₹22,000 Activities~₹8,420 Food, 3 days~₹4,500 Local travel~₹3,600 ~₹98,520 suggested · ₹150,000 budget Peak bloom · early April14places across 3 days, each one movable by asking How it works01Say where you are goingTell your guide the place, or just the mood. It asks three quick things (where from, where to, how many days). Dates, budget, pace and interests are optional. 02Get a draft, or build it togetherGenerate the whole itinerary in one go, or plan one day at a time while your guide suggests places that fit the day and the budget. 03Open the Trip StudioOne page for the whole trip: the day plan, a hand-drawn sketchbook, a map, a 3D route, and the weather and public holidays for your dates. 04Change it by asking, then take it with youSay “move the market to day 1” and it is done, with a receipt of what changed. Export a PDF, a calendar, map files or the budget as a spreadsheet. What the agent actually doesMost planners write you a list. This one keeps a plan you can change.Four things follow from that difference. Keep scrolling: this section moves sideways. Scroll Every change leaves a receipt01Ask for a change and it happensSay “move Nishiki Market to day 2” and the plan changes, the studio follows, and a receipt under the reply lists exactly what changed. If a day gets too full or the budget is passed, it tells you instead of refusing. Drawn live, page by page02A guide who draws your tripPick a guide and they sketch each day on paper as the plan takes shape: the places, the order, the weather, the public holiday. Change something in the chat and the page is redrawn while you watch. Map and 3D in one studio03The itinerary is a map, not a listEvery stop sits on a real map and in a 3D route you can orbit, with photos, what is nearby, and the forecast or the season’s typical weather for your dates. Suggested first, then yours to accept04A budget you can see, not guessSet a target in the brief, or just say it. The budget planner suggests typical costs from traveler reports, row by row, and nothing counts toward your total until you accept it. While it plansYour guide says what it is doing as it goes: researching stops, reading what travelers recommend, checking the weather and public holidays for your dates, then writing the days. The draft streams in, and the route draws itself alongside. WeatherA forecast near your dates, the month’s typical beyond Traveler tipsLinked to the post they came from tripverse · kyoto, 3 days YouPlan 3 days in Kyoto from Delhi. I love food and old temples. TripVerseI’ve put together a balanced, three-day itinerary for your trip to Kyoto. Since you’re traveling in mid-October, you’ll be there during the pleasant autumn season, though October is part of the rainy season, so I’ve built in some flexibility. Read your brief3 days · 2 travelers · food, temples Researched possible stopsKyoto, from Delhi Checked your datesTypical for October · Sports Day on day 1 Writing your day-by-day draftDay 2 of 3 Drawing the sketchbookQueued Day Planned Date Places D1 Fushimi Inari Taisha, Takashimaya food hall Mon 12 Oct, holiday 2 D2 Arashiyama Bamboo Grove, Kiyomizu-dera, Nishiki Market Tue 13 Oct 8 D3 Okochi-sanso Villa, Nishijin, Uji Wed 14 Oct 4 Places to start Explore destinations KyotoUKY Temple districts, kaiseki, autumn maples 4 nightsJapan PortoOPO Douro riverfront, tiled facades, port cellars 3 nightsPortugal PraguePRG Old Town rooftops

